      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -284
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Gradients = interpolated palettes\n\n`color/gradient` reads a Spread<Color> and a t ∈ [0, 1]; it linearly interpolates between adjacent stops. Smoother than CycleSpread when you want a continuous transition.\n\nMouseX → t → sampled gradient → fill colour.",
        "width": 440,
        "height": 220
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Gradients = interpolated palettes\n\n`color/gradient` reads a Spread<Color> and a t ∈ [0, 1]; it linearly interpolates between adjacent stops. Smoother than CycleSpread when you want a continuous transition.\n\nMouseX → t → sampled gradient → fill colour.",
